:[{"type":"text","text":"Landmarks for A* search by the ALT method (Goldberg and Harrelson, “Computing the shortest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"path: A* search meets graph theory”, SODA 2005): a few vertices chosen far apart, the distance"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from and to each of them stored for every vertex, and each query an A* search whose estimate of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a vertex’s remaining distance is the largest lower bound the triangle inequality gives from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any landmark, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"d(L, t) − d(L, v)"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"d(v, L) − d(t, L)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"ALTLandmarks","identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ALTLandmarks"}}}